1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,440
Many years ago, mankind faced a divine fury.

2
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:16,840
In an event known as the Day of the Cataclysm,

3
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,040
our entire world was burned.

4
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:24,120
The fire raged with an intensity that threatened to reduce mankind to ash.

5
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,500
The places they lived, the languages they spoke,

6
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:29,220
the culture they had built.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,480
None could escape its wrath.

8
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,080
Their base is one ramshackle shack.

9
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:42,600
Hello, Lieutenant Karim.

10
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:44,000
It's good to see you.

11
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:45,460
What brings you all here?

12
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:48,140
Tamaki, it looks like you're doing well here.

13
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:48,720
I'm glad.

14
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,460
We came here to compare notes on the Evangelist.

15
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:54,260
Hopefully we can all work together from this point forward.

16
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:57,080
If we end up going after the Whiteclad,

17
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:59,920
then I'm probably going to have to fight Cho again.

18
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,680
Stop spacing out and say something!

19
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:06,860
How did this happen?

20
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,800
You may not be the steed fated to carry me,

21
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:14,020
but you're still my comrade in arms.

22
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,180
We've been through a lot.

23
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:18,220
It's good to have you back, Silboro.

24
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:23,340
Could you maybe not put up freaky fake animal heads on our wall?

25
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:26,240
This Celestial Charger just returned to Earth.

26
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:28,660
Thanks to Vulcan's miraculous work.

27
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:30,180
Yeah, it's a donkey.

28
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:32,640
Are you really okay with this, Lieutenant?

29
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,600
Arthur, get back to work.

30
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,260
I'm guessing that hat came from Vulcan, too?

31
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:40,240
I found it by my desk this morning.

32
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:41,520
Those big horns.

33
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:43,260
Don't they get in the way a bit?

34
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,220
They don't interfere with my work.

35
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:46,800
No offense, Lieutenant,

36
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,960
but when it comes to fashion, you're oblivious.

37
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:51,180
You want me to help you pick out clothes sometime?

38
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,320
I wouldn't trust you to pick out anything

39
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,860
that didn't come from a fairy tale.

40
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:57,620
Well, you couldn't look worse than you do with horns.

41
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:59,760
Okay, that's enough idle chatter.

42
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:03,880
I feel like they do interfere with your work, sir.

43
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:04,240
Ugh!

44
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:05,880
Ugh!

45
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:35,860
Ugh!

46
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:40,840
Take what you got and leave now

47
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,800
You're wearing out your welcome

48
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:46,440
No one here wants to see you here, yeah

49
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,840
Think that you won from day one

50
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,900
But the devil will come

51
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:54,480
You know just why he wants you, don't you?

52
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,540
You're crooked, this iron

53
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:58,560
It doesn't feel so right

54
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,540
Missguided, defighted

55
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,520
And the final will raise it

56
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:04,220
You're starting a fight

57
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:06,740
You're trying to watch it burn

58
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:09,680
Try to save yourself like you always do

59
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:13,080
Every bridge we've built

60
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:15,500
You think it's just a burning death

61
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,880
Just burn it down

62
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:20,960
When everything is gone

63
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,560
You wish you only heard us out

64
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,240
Heard us out

65
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:28,940
Screaming, my time

66
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:33,040
My time

67
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:46,440
Thank you, miss

68
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,600
That's kind of you

69
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,620
I made it with my guts, sir

70
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:53,620
What gives, Obi?

71
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:58,280
Why do you have Iris doing the work of a common housemaid right now?

72
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,980
No, it's okay, sister

73
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,280
I offered to do this

74
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,540
But hey

75
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:04,940
What are you sitting like that for?

76
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:09,420
I'm sitting up here because I refuse to be placed at the same level as this gravel

77
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:11,900
Would you feel better if I sat on the floor then?

78
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:12,520
I would

79
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,840
Go ahead and get down there

80
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,560
What's the holdup?

81
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:18,420
You offered, so hop to it

82
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:23,360
Damn it

83
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,460
I wasn't actually offering to

84
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:26,940
It was just a little joke quip

85
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:30,340
All right

86
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:33,300
Let's skip the formalities and get right to the meat of it

87
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:36,080
We'll share what information we've scrounged up

88
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:37,600
See if that gives us any clues

89
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:40,700
Then decide how to deal with the white clad moving forward

90
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:43,740
My company didn't think the white clad existed until now

91
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,760
So we're still playing catch-up

92
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,860
Benny asked me to come on his behalf

93
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:49,680
But I won't have much to contribute

94
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:53,060
White clad operatives have made countless infernals

95
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:56,700
They're especially likely to be the orchestrators of any mass combustion events

96
00:04:57,260 --> 00:05:00,640
Rekka Hoshimiya wasn't turning those kids to cause chaos

97
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:04,920
He wanted to find a compatible host for the so-called pilot light

98
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:07,700
So those bugs do more than create infernals

99
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:11,400
They're also used to find people with a special ability

100
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:14,160
Dr. Giovanni's a white clad

101
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:16,760
And he was looking for the key to Amaterasu

102
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:20,680
I guess these guys have plans for our perpetual power plant

103
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:24,140
The media's been told that the man who attacked Vulcan

104
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:28,040
Was actually an imposter wearing a mask that looked like Giovanni's

105
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:32,380
But the man Company 3 sent to their press conference was the real fake

106
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:34,480
Hijima wanted to prevent a scandal

107
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,440
So they made a new captain

108
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:40,240
Vulcan's seen Giovanni's face and he said that wasn't him

109
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:43,260
So we're safe to assume the real Giovanni took off

110
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:46,980
I hear that quite a few soldiers have suddenly disappeared from the third

111
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:50,260
It seems likely that all of them were white clad spies as well

112
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:53,680
They've probably all returned to the Evangelist by now

113
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:56,760
I have no idea if Hijima itself has been compromised

114
00:05:56,760 --> 00:06:00,520
But as long as the third has its backing, they're out of the government's reach

115
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:04,680
The longer we wait, the bolder and more radical the white clad are gonna get

116
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:07,340
Till we know how to root out their spies

117
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:09,740
We should look for their base and hit them directly

118
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:13,820
I agree and I've already got my man Leek looking into the base's location

119
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:21,520
So tell me, how's the special fire force been treating you?

120
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:23,980
The gig's been downright convenient for me

121
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:26,680
Got me permission to come to this crime scene

122
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:35,320
Is that really all you need to find the white clad base?

123
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:37,320
Nah, even I need more than this

124
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:41,420
Do you believe Leek is trustworthy?

125
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:44,520
So far at least, he's doing good work for us

126
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:49,740
Once we've pinpointed the location of the Evangelist

127
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,720
The Eighth will move in and take him out

128
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,500
Is the Eighth up to that task?

129
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:56,300
About half of your company's fighters are rookies, correct?

130
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,740
It'd be a shame if some meathead led them to their doom

131
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:04,820
You might find the Evangelist's base

132
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:07,680
But the Eighth isn't strong enough to attack it yet

133
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:09,520
Are the white clad that strong?

134
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,360
You have no idea

135
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:15,560
Having seen their commander's power first hand

136
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,920
I believe it comes from a direct link to the Evangelist

137
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,540
An Adola link, huh?

138
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:25,300
So what does the Eighth need to do to get strong enough?

139
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:27,880
Our company's rookies are fine soldiers

140
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:30,820
They've got solid instincts and powerful abilities

141
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:33,240
But they still have room to grow

142
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,320
How can we help them do that quickly?

143
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,460
When I saw them sparring at the first

144
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:39,960
They struck me as green and wet behind the ears

145
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,560
They've got first-class, top-notch powers

146
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,440
But they need more combat training

147
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,140
Combat training, eh?

148
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:49,460
I just happen to know the best fighter in the entire force

149
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:51,800
Why don't you send them back with me?

150
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:56,900
What matters most is that our Devil gets stronger

151
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:59,780
Can you think of a way to upgrade his flames?

152
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:01,400
I might have an idea

153
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:05,840
But whether or not he catches up to you and show

154
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,000
That depends on him

155
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:13,140
Gondro, what's going on?

156
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:15,520
Huh?

157
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:18,660
And why should I agree to babysit their rookies?

158
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:21,800
Say what?

159
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,040
I owe them?

160
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:24,480
Oh yeah

161
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,780
Guess I do

162
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:34,760
Hey, Captain Shinmon

163
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,560
It's me, Shinra Kusikabe

164
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:44,180
Um, is everything okay, Captain?

165
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:46,320
In a real fight, you'd be dead

166
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:48,520
Okay, step right up, people!

167
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:49,940
Lesson one

168
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:52,400
You never know when a foe might strike

169
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,180
So stay sharp

170
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:55,540
Dumbass

171
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:58,400
What part of stay sharp did you miss?

172
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,140
Who's dumb now?

173
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:07,060
Iron Medillo

174
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:09,300
The magnetic extinguishing ball

175
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,460
So how does it work?

176
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,280
I'll let you see for yourself

177
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:18,040
And there it goes

178
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:20,400
It hits the fire with a quick magnetic blast

179
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,700
And the flames sputter out a second later

180
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:24,120
Way to go, Vulcan

181
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,920
An unpowered person like me

182
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:27,300
Could make good use of that

183
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:29,780
Shinra and Arthur are getting special training

184
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:30,820
In Asakusa, right?

185
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,580
I don't want to get shown up

186
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,780
So I figured I'd make us some new tools

187
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:48,900
You aren't relaxing, are you?

188
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:51,120
There are no rules in a real fight

189
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,900
Which means you can't predict when something might happen

190
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:57,020
Getting tired?

191
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:58,920
Y-yes, sir

192
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:01,640
That's because you know your life isn't on the line

193
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:04,980
You need to act like it is and channel all that tension you're feeling

194
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,360
Let that stress heighten your awareness

195
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,300
Feel life around you

196
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,600
Not just your allies

197
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:12,080
But your enemies, too

198
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:14,900
Focus on the lives at stake in a fight

199
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:16,840
And you can turn stress into a tool

200
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,740
So we should value life

201
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:20,720
Channel it

202
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:22,600
When you're feeling alive in that way

203
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,660
Self-defense becomes reflexive

204
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:26,180
All right

205
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:27,880
Let's get some practice in

206
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:30,300
Come at me like I'm out for your lives

207
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:36,920
Ah, so it begins

208
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:37,880
Kill him, Waka!

209
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:45,160
That's enough

210
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,260
Already?

211
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:49,620
Your technique isn't bad, but you're not about to hit me

212
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:52,520
All of your attacks are completely predictable

213
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,820
You need to shake things up somehow

214
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,420
And how do I do that?

215
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:59,820
Well, I think you need what I call

216
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:01,800
A finishing move

217
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,300
Like an ultimate

218
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:07,880
That's what happens when you let your guard down

219
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:12,360
What you need is a finishing move that capitalizes on your speed advantage

220
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,460
Well said, Captain Sheenmon

221
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:16,420
You're not just crazy strong

222
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:17,560
You're perceptive

223
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:17,960
Huh?

224
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:19,000
Hi

225
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,060
It's nice to meet you

226
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:22,480
I'm the head of the eight's one-man science team

227
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:23,920
And I'm here to crash your party

228
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,300
My name is Victor Leet

229
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:28,960
I've thought of a way to help Shinra give himself a power boost

230
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:32,720
I'm gonna need help to demonstrate

231
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:33,420
Hey, Captain!

232
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,960
Could you help me out for a second?

233
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:36,800
Depends on what you want

234
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:39,400
I want to show Shinra how jet propulsion works

235
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:43,800
If he can emulate it, he should get a lot more burst firepower out of those V to his

236
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:47,380
If he compresses his fire as he emits it

237
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:49,720
The thrust he gets will straight up skyrocket

238
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:54,120
So basically, you want me to show him how to tighten a flame?

239
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,080
Yes, I do

240
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:59,160
Will this be enough firepower?

241
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,220
Yes, it will

242
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:12,480
That was awesome!

243
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:17,800
See, when you fly normally, your flames get pushed out in all sorts of useless directions

244
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:21,400
Rain them in a bit, and you can take advantage of all that raw power you've got

245
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:23,880
If you can do like the captain showed you

246
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:26,400
And condense your flame so it only shoots one way

247
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,360
It should increase your speed by a good margin

248
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:32,600
And if I can do that, then I'll have my ultimate attack

249
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:46,860
I want you to focus on making that finishing move of yours work, Shinra

250
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:47,660
Sir

251
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:50,620
Arthur, your power is already a finishing move

252
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:53,120
Let's just keep sparring, work on the basics

253
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:55,120
Come try to kill me

254
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:58,620
Alrighty then, let's watch this cookie crumble

255
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:02,340
I have to say, you've got a different air than the rest of the 8th

256
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:05,580
I heard that you were sent there by Hajima Industries

257
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,620
A different air, huh?

258
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:09,640
You trying to say I'm too smart for them?

259
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:11,220
Too strange

260
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:14,380
Try anything funny with them and I'll dump you in the sea

261
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:16,240
Why does everyone think I'm a traitor?

262
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:17,580
What did I do?

263
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:36,640
I fly with my toes

264
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:38,960
Fine-tune my positioning with minor movements

265
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,680
If I don't pay attention to that, I lose my balance

266
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:45,980
But when I'm trying to squeeze my flame tighter, I really want to scrunch up my feet

267
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:53,940
Since I haven't even made it work once yet, there's no point thinking

268
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:55,880
Just need to plug on for now

269
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,720
I think he might be on to something

270
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:00,940
You can deal with most problems by saying one of two things

271
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:03,120
Time to give up or whatever, just do it

272
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:06,960
For a brilliant scientist, that's a real simple way to think

273
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:09,120
Eh, sometimes thinking's pointless

274
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:12,960
If you're at the start line of a race against rivals you don't know on a track you've never seen

275
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,380
You gotta start running

276
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:18,400
The toughest problems are solved by throwing effort at the wall and seeing if it breaks

277
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,740
That's certainly a surprise

278
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:23,820
I think we might have something in common after all

279
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:29,480
Captain Shinmon has perfect control of his flames

280
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:31,040
How does he do it?

281
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:34,260
There's got to be some kind of secret

282
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:57,700
I've told you before and I'll tell you now

283
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,500
We do not play with fire here

284
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,960
Now what can I do to help you remember?

285
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:04,560
It isn't what it looks like, sir

286
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:07,400
Spudder and Flare have an important mission this time

287
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:11,120
Has your obsession with fairy tales finally driven you mad?

288
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:13,160
She's telling you the truth, Lieutenant

289
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:17,260
I made Maki some new equipment and it needs Spudder and Flare to operate

290
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,300
What?

291
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,780
I gave the twin hover units a name

292
00:15:20,780 --> 00:15:21,820
It's Tekkyo

293
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:27,900
They use Spudder and Flare as power sources

294
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:31,440
Which means Maki can use your second-gen powers to move them

295
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:33,380
What exactly do they do?

296
00:15:33,780 --> 00:15:35,160
They're pretty much flying hammers

297
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:39,880
I know a lot of pyrokinetic enemies are flame resistant, so I figured these might help

298
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:46,600
So what do you think?

299
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,460
I think you three just passed your flight test

300
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:52,400
Then the Spud Flare witch is ready for action

301
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,500
Yeah, that isn't what we're calling him

302
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:55,840
The name's Tekkyo

303
00:15:55,840 --> 00:16:01,160
Many years ago, mankind faced a divine fury

304
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:04,200
In an event known as the Day of the Cataclysm

305
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,320
Our world was bathed in fire

306
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:10,860
The fire raged with an intensity that threatened to reduce mankind to ash

307
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:12,260
The places they lived

308
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:13,420
The languages they spoke

309
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:14,840
The culture they had built

310
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,120
None could escape it

311
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:17,300
Come on

312
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:18,600
Tighten up

313
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,120
I got plenty of fire

314
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,260
I just need to pinch it

315
00:16:22,260 --> 00:16:30,500
Your flames haven't changed at all

316
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:33,020
Like all you can do is switch between gross faces

317
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:33,820
What?

318
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:35,740
Was the face I made that weird?

319
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:37,800
If by weird you mean disgusting, sure

320
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,940
The fugliest pucker face I've seen

321
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:42,080
Guess this gesture won't work either then

322
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:45,080
I could try the one that Captain Obi likes to do

323
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:46,640
Rock and roll!

324
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:51,980
The hell was that?

325
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,620
Did Shinra just rip a huge fart through his feet?

326
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:55,540
Huh?

327
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:57,000
Huh?

328
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:01,100
Now it's you who's not on guard!

329
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:04,440
Doesn't count as a sneak attack if you announce it

330
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:07,620
Good try though

331
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:09,540
You've got your head in the right place now

332
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:10,860
Think he's dead

333
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:13,600
Shinra, show me what you're doing

334
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:17,120
I saw you make gestures with your hands

335
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,380
When you powered up your flames

336
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:20,560
So I thought I'd try it out for myself

337
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:23,000
I got the last one I tried from Captain Obi

338
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,320
And I don't know

339
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:26,580
I feel like this one might have done something

340
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:34,840
No dice

341
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:38,120
Take off your gloves so I can see what you're trying to do

342
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:38,980
Yes sir

343
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:41,900
You saw me using hand forms

344
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,380
Which are also known as kata

345
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:47,360
They were commonly used by the martial artists of old Japan

346
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,340
There are many

347
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:51,580
I usually use this one to control my fire

348
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:55,320
But every single one of these kata is meant to have a different effect

349
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:58,640
There's even one that channels power to the user's feet

350
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:00,420
It's called tiger crusher

351
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:01,580
Watch closely

352
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:05,820
Put your index finger on the base of your thumb

353
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:08,760
And bend your thumb pushing it towards the base of your pinky

354
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:12,220
By using these kata

355
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:16,160
You can channel your energy or ki into certain parts of your body

356
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:18,160
This also affects your flames

357
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,760
Amazing

358
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,180
I had no idea

359
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:22,400
Yeah

360
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,540
Good luck

361
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,480
Thank you for the help sir

362
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:29,460
We've got more training to do

363
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:30,340
Up and at them

364
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:37,680
So I bend both my index finger and thumb inward

365
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:41,160
Focus on channeling energy into my feet

366
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:53,520
I think that was it

367
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:55,060
My fire compressed

368
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:57,200
I was about to blast off like a rocket

369
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:59,540
The tiger crush is amazing

370
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:05,440
So this is how my power works

371
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:08,280
By channeling the flow of my body's energy

372
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:10,320
I can master my flames

373
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:17,580
I feel the heat in my feet

374
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:20,320
The shape of my hand

375
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:22,900
Pushes all my strength down

376
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:25,760
Sho needs my help

377
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,400
I need to reach him as fast as possible

378
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,920
Faster

379
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,480
Faster

380
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:40,260
Okay

381
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:43,960
I think I see what Joker sees in you now

382
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:47,120
Pretty impressive

383
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:48,800
Hey

384
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,240
I'll give you credit for being quiet that time

385
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:51,860
Sheena

386
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:54,940
Use that speed boost to come after me now

387
00:19:54,940 --> 00:20:02,060
Benny was really dreading this

388
00:20:02,060 --> 00:20:04,480
I'm glad to see he's having fun now

389
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:05,200
Is he?

390
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:07,720
It's hard to tell from looking at his face

391
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:12,120
Two fighters who are worth training have come his way

392
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:15,720
I bet you Benny's ecstatic right now

393
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:20,720
A true knight never surrenders

394
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:23,200
It looks like your friend's pretty worn out

395
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:25,380
I think we better call it a day

396
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:29,720
It looked like you got knocked around a lot

397
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:30,340
You good?

398
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:31,160
Of course

399
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:32,220
Knights are resilient

400
00:20:32,220 --> 00:20:33,460
So tell me

401
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:35,640
Do you have a name for that new finishing move?

402
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:36,500
Oh yeah

403
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,580
My ultimate attack

404
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:38,180
Stay sharp

405
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:44,360
So what's this move of yours called?

406
00:20:44,360 --> 00:20:45,560
The kicker mandate

407
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:46,440
Overruled

408
00:20:46,440 --> 00:21:07,280
What do you think?

409
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:08,100
They any good?

410
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,940
Yeah, but there's still just a couple of kids

411
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:18,800
Too shaky for their own good

412
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:33,900
We'll make a proto-nationalist swordsman of you yet, kid

413
00:21:33,900 --> 00:21:36,440
That single-edge blade isn't like yours

414
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:37,780
It works differently

415
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:39,520
It's own technique

416
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:41,680
But it never hurts to learn, right?

417
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:53,080
Okay, you did good

418
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:54,980
Would have hit me if I hadn't known

419
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,960
Use it wisely

420
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:57,800
Sir!

421
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:00,580
I heard about your brother, Sho

422
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:02,860
How he's the only family you have

423
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:04,880
Keep him safe, okay?

424
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:05,800
Thank you, sir

425
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:06,680
Will do

426
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:10,300
I'm coming, Sho

427
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:37,300
You're soif

428
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:53,660
指を立ててきた奴が その爪で誰かを守る

429
00:22:53,660 --> 00:22:59,020
武器は傷と立てる代わる 人生なんてそんなもんなんじゃないの

430
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:04,200
ずっと消えそうで 消えないような 誰にも知れない

431
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:34,180
I'll see you next time.

432
00:23:34,200 --> 00:24:04,180
I'll see you next time.

